WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.550
Today's chemical is isopropyl alcohol, or IPA, CAS number 67-63-0.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:12.060
IPA is a highly flammable liquid with a flash point of about 12 degrees Celsius.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.860
Vapors can spread along the floor and flash back.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.480
It seriously irritates the eyes and airways.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:23.220
It may harm fertility or an unborn child, and repeated exposure can damage organs.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.820
Keep away from heat and sparks, ground equipment, and never eat, drink or smoke while handling.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.700
Use good ventilation, and store it sealed in a cool, locked area away from food.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:39.360
Wear gloves, safety goggles and protective clothing, plus a gas mask when exposure is high.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.610
Eyes and skin: rinse with water and remove contaminated clothing.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.190
If swallowed, get medical help now. Do not induce vomiting.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.970
Spill: remove ignition sources and absorb with dry sand.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:54.500
Fire: use alcohol foam, CO2 or water spray.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:00.070
On the label, pictograms show the hazard type. The signal word Danger means serious risk.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:04.870
Hazard statements explain the risk; precautionary statements tell you what to do.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.910
The full MSDS has 16 sections. Check it at your workplace before handling.
